      "id": "y9rvbbr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. BASIC CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "HCF (Highest Common Factor) and LCM (Least Common Multiple) can be found using Prime Factorisation or Division Method.",
        "For any two given numbers, Product of Two Numbers = HCF × LCM.",
        "HCF of Fractions = (HCF of Numerators) / (LCM of Denominators).",
        "LCM of Fractions = (LCM of Numerators) / (HCF of Denominators).",
        "Word problems involving maximum capacity or division usually require finding HCF, whereas problems involving simultaneous occurrences require LCM."
      ],
      "id": "rbr9smk"
    },
